outcome.text:
{
  "problem_statement": "Within the author-created simulation, workshop logs record missing chargers on two occasions, with counts of three and four. This suggests a recurring charger-availability problem worth investigating, but both logs come from one coordinator and do not establish independent corroboration or real-world need (C1, C2).",
  "affected_users": [
    "Simulated workshop staff who need chargers; the coordinator records the shortages. Specific staff roles and the number affected are unknown (C1)."
  ],
  "observable_problem": "Two logs report three and four missing chargers. Whether these represent distinct chargers, overlapping unresolved shortages, borrowing failures or other causes is unknown; the counts should not be summed as seven distinct losses (C1, C2).",
  "urgency": {
    "frequency": "Reported in two logs; dates, observation intervals and the rate of recurrence are not supplied (C1, C2).",
    "severity": "unknown",
    "claim_refs": ["C1", "C2"]
  },
  "workarounds": [
    {
      "description": "The coordinator records missing chargers in workshop logs. This is an observed monitoring practice, not evidence of an effective recovery or prevention workaround.",
      "claim_refs": ["C1", "C2"]
    }
  ],
  "alternatives": [
    {
      "description": "Investigate a non-software approach using tagged containers and designated charger-return locations. Tagged containers reportedly reduced misplaced items at a simulated borrowing desk, but their effectiveness for workshop chargers is untested.",
      "claim_refs": ["C3"]
    },
    {
      "description": "Before selecting an intervention, have an authorized human reconcile the two logs with a physical inventory and clarify whether chargers are borrowed, misplaced or unavailable for another reason. This is a proposed diagnostic step, not a completed check.",
      "claim_refs": ["C1", "C2"]
    }
  ],
  "software_hypothesis": null,
  "cross_field": {
    "from_field": "borrowing logistics",
    "to_field": "workshop maintenance",
    "transferred_mechanism": "Use tagged containers to give chargers identifiable storage and return destinations, potentially making misplaced items and incomplete returns easier to detect.",
    "why_it_transfers": "Both settings can involve movable items that must return to identifiable locations. The borrowing-desk observation provides a candidate physical organization mechanism, but this explanation and its applicability depend on charger misplacement or return failures actually causing the workshop shortages.",
    "claim_refs": ["C1", "C3"]
  },
  "cross_field_absent_reason": null,
  "evidence_strength": "exploratory",
  "gaps": [
    "Scope: all evidence is synthetic. Internal support does not establish real-world need, customer validation or intervention benefit.",
    "Source independence: C1 and C2 explicitly identify one coordinator as the author of both logs. C3 does not independently corroborate workshop shortages.",
    "Frequency and impact: observation dates, inventory size, shortage duration, workflow disruption and replacement costs are absent.",
    "Causal uncertainty: the packet does not establish that borrowing or incorrect returns cause missing chargers. A different cause would change the recommendation.",
    "Accessible data are limited to the supplied observations. No inventory records, item-level histories or intervention trials are available (C1, C2).",
    "A prospective outcome could be the number of missing chargers at consistently scheduled inventory checks, with inventory size recorded. No such measurement protocol or intervention result is supplied.",
    "Existing alternatives review was limited to the packet: its catalog is empty, and C3 supplies only a tagged-container approach. No external search, tool comparison or software-benefit assessment was possible.",
    "Checks actually executed: reviewed C1–C3 for observations, independence, causal support and transfer evidence. No tools, external searches, trials or outreach were used.",
    "Decision/status: bounded discovery assessment completed; intervention selection remains deferred. The next permitted action is to return this assessment, not conduct a trial or obtain additional access.",
    "Usage: the supplied runtime specifies no new metered spending but provides no actual usage or billing figures."
  ]
}
